  Surveys of topos methods in machine learning emphasise that sheaf and topos language naturally express how local interventions affect global behaviour, how invariances are organised, and how internal logical structure can be extracted. Hallucination, in this reading, is a failure of a global section to exist, or a quotient taken with respect to the wrong equivalence relation — exactly the diagnosis offered in the earlier notes.

